{"name":"Arabian Silk","hex":"#786e97","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"silk","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fine fiber excreted by the silkworm or other arthropod (such as a spider).","A thread or yarn made from silk fibers."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To develop silk.","To remove the silk from (corn)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silk"}],"entries":[{"title":"Arabian Peninsula","blocks":[{"text":"The Arabian Peninsula, or simply Arabia, is a peninsula in West Asia. It accounts for the majority of the land situated on the Arabian plate. With an area of 3,237,500 km2 (1.25 million mi2), it is the world's largest peninsula—roughly comparable in size to India. Nine countries are located on the Arabian Peninsula: Bahrain, Kuwait, Oman, Qatar, Saudi Arabia, the United Arab Emirates, and Yemen, as well as the southern halves of Iraq and Jordan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Arabian_Peninsula_dust_SeaWiFS.jpg/330px-Arabian_Peninsula_dust_SeaWiFS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arabian_Peninsula","wikidata":"Q31945"},{"title":"Silk","blocks":[{"text":"Silk is a natural protein fiber, some forms of which can be woven or knitted into textiles. The protein fiber of silk is composed mainly of fibroin (75-80%) and a smaller coating of sericin (20-25%). It is most commonly produced from the cocoons of certain insect larvae. The best-known silk is obtained from the cocoons of the larvae of the mulberry silkworm Bombyx mori, which are reared in captivity (sericulture)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Silk_raw_01a.jpg/330px-Silk_raw_01a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silk","wikidata":"Q37681"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Near_East_in_10